        <p class="lede">
          Micellar casein protein powder is casein filtered out of skim milk with its natural micelle structure intact, so it thickens in the stomach and releases amino acids over several hours. Whether that matters depends on when you eat your protein and how much you get in a day. This guide covers the label differences, the timing evidence, third-party testing and cost per 25 g.
        </p>

